    "id": 73,
    "verse_number": 26,
    "chapter_number": 2,
    "slug": "chapter-2-verse-26",
    "text": "अथ चैनं नित्यजातं नित्यं वा मन्यसे मृतम्।\n\nतथापि त्वं महाबाहो नैवं शोचितुमर्हसि।।2.26।।\n ",
    "transliteration": "atha chainaṁ nitya-jātaṁ nityaṁ vā manyase mṛitam\ntathāpi tvaṁ mahā-bāho naivaṁ śhochitum arhasi\n",
    "word_meanings": "atha—if, however; cha—and; enam—this soul; nitya-jātam—taking constant birth; nityam—always; vā—or; manyase—you think; mṛitam—dead; tathā api—even then; tvam—you; mahā-bāho—mighty-armed one, Arjun; na—not; evam—like this; śhochitum—grieve; arhasi—befitting\n",
    "translations": [
      {
        "id": 505,
        "description": "।।2.26।। हे महाबाहो ! अगर तुम इस देहीको नित्य पैदा होनेवाला अथवा नित्य मरनेवाला भी मानो, तो भी तुम्हें इस प्रकार शोक नहीं करना चाहिये।\n ",
        "authorName": "Swami Ramsukhdas",
        "language": "hindi"
      },
      {
        "id": 506,
        "description": "।।2.26।। और यदि तुम आत्मा को नित्य जन्मने और नित्य मरने वाला मानो तो भी,  हे महाबाहो !  इस प्रकार शोक करना तुम्हारे लिए उचित नहीं है।।\n ",
        "authorName": "Swami Tejomayananda",
        "language": "hindi"
      },
      {
        "id": 507,
        "description": "Or, if you consider this self as constantly being born and constantly dying, O mighty-armed one, it still does not become you to feel grief.",
        "authorName": "Swami Adidevananda",
        "language": "english"
      },
      {
        "id": 508,
        "description": "On the other hand, if you think this One is born continually or constantly dies, even then, O mighty-armed one, you should not grieve.",
        "authorName": "Swami Gambirananda",
        "language": "english"
      },
      {
        "id": 509,
        "description": "But even if thou thinkest of It as constantly being born and constantly dying, even then, O mighty-armed one, thou shouldst not grieve.",
        "authorName": "Swami Sivananda",
        "language": "english"
      },
      {
        "id": 510,
        "description": "On the other hand, if you deem this as being born constantly or as dying constantly, even then, O mighty-armed one, you should not lament.",
        "authorName": "Dr. S. Sankaranarayan",
        "language": "english"
      },
      {
        "id": 511,
        "description": "Even if thou thinkest of it as constantly being born and constantly dying, O Mighty Man, thou still hast no cause to grieve.",
        "authorName": "Shri Purohit Swami",
        "language": "english"
      }
    ],
    "commentaries": []
