    "chapter_number": 4,
    "slug": "chapter-4-verse-19",
    "text": "यस्य सर्वे समारम्भाः कामसङ्कल्पवर्जिताः।\n\nज्ञानाग्निदग्धकर्माणं तमाहुः पण्डितं बुधाः।।4.19।।\n ",
    "transliteration": "yasya sarve samārambhāḥ kāma-saṅkalpa-varjitāḥ\njñānāgni-dagdha-karmāṇaṁ tam āhuḥ paṇḍitaṁ budhāḥ\n\n",
    "word_meanings": "yasya—whose; sarve—every; samārambhāḥ—undertakings; kāma—desire for material pleasures; saṅkalpa—resolve; varjitāḥ—devoid of; jñāna—divine knowledge; agni—in the fire; dagdha—burnt; karmāṇam—actions; tam—him; āhuḥ—address; paṇḍitam—a sage; budhāḥ—the wise\n\n",
    "translations": [
      {
        "id": 1261,
        "description": "।।4.19।। जिसके सम्पूर्ण कर्मोंके आरम्भ संकल्प और कामनासे रहित हैं तथा जिसके सम्पूर्ण कर्म ज्ञानरूपी अग्निसे जल गये हैं, उसको ज्ञानिजन भी पण्डित (बुद्धिमान्) कहते हैं। ",
        "authorName": "Swami Ramsukhdas",
        "language": "hindi"
      },
      {
        "id": 1262,
        "description": "।।4.19।। जिसके समस्त कार्य कामना और संकल्प से रहित हैं,  ऐसे उस ज्ञानरूप अग्नि के द्वारा भस्म हुये कर्मों वाले पुरुष को ज्ञानीजन पण्डित कहते हैं।।\n ",
        "authorName": "Swami Tejomayananda",
        "language": "hindi"
      },
      {
        "id": 1263,
        "description": "He whose every undertaking is free from desire and delusive identification (of the body with the self), whose actions are burned up in the fire of knowledge—the wise describe him as a sage.",
        "authorName": "Swami Adidevananda",
        "language": "english"
      },
      {
        "id": 1264,
        "description": "The wise call him learned whose actions are all devoid of desires and their thoughts, and whose actions have been burned away by the fire of wisdom.",
        "authorName": "Swami Gambirananda",
        "language": "english"
      },
      {
        "id": 1265,
        "description": "He whose undertakings are all devoid of desires and selfish purposes, and whose actions have been burned by the fire of knowledge, the wise call him a sage.",
        "authorName": "Swami Sivananda",
        "language": "english"
      },
      {
        "id": 1266,
        "description": "He whose every exertion is devoid of intention for desirable objects, and whose actions are burnt up by the fire of wisdom—the wise call such a person a man of learning.",
        "authorName": "Dr. S. Sankaranarayan",
        "language": "english"
      },
      {
        "id": 1267,
        "description": "The wise call him a sage, for whatever he undertakes is free from the motive of desire, and his deeds are purified by the fire of wisdom.",
        "authorName": "Shri Purohit Swami",
        "language": "english"
      }
    ],
    "commentaries": []
